Added `invoke` tasks for the containerlab lab - `lab-up`, `lab-down`, `lab-populate`, `lab-consumer`, `lab-break`, `lab-events` and `lab-console` - and an `eventconsumer` task for running the consumer against any configured broker. The lab's compose overlay is added automatically when `EVENT_TRACKER_LAB` is set, so no `invoke.yml` editing is needed.
The containerlab population script now assigns fabric addresses read from each node's own startup configuration and cables every link between two devices, alongside the management addresses it already assigned.
`generate_nautobot_event_tracker_test_data` now gives its demo devices a management address from TEST-NET-1 as their primary IP and cables them to each other.
